 1/4 of the same cake?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "1/2", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "1/4", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m3u06s1p06", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many quarters make a whole?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u06s1p07", "type": "num", "prompt": "A pizza in 6 equal slices; 5 are eaten. Fraction left? Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.16666666666666666, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 1e-06, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u06s1p08", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Non-unit fraction?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "3/10", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "1/10", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "adv": [{"id": "m3u06s1a01", "type": "explain", "prompt": "* Advanced. A square is cut into 4 equal triangles. Is each 1/4? Explain.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "yes", "kw": ["\\byes\\b"]}, {"pt": "equal", "kw": ["equal|same"]}], "need": 2, "model": "Yes – the 4 parts are equal, so each is 1/4, even though they are triangles.", "hint": "", "reason": "Yes – the 4 parts are equal, so each is 1/4, even though they are triangles."}, {"id": "m3u06s1a02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "* Advanced. Order from smallest: 1/2, 1/10, 1/5", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "1/10, 1/5, 1/2", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "1/2, 1/5, 1/10", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m3u06s1a03", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. 12 equal parts, 4 shaded. Fraction shaded? Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 1e-06, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "4/12.", "reason": ""}], "more": [{"id": "m3u06s1m01", "type": "num", "prompt": "2 parts, 1 shaded? Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 1e-06, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u06s1m02", "type": "num", "prompt": "4 parts, 3 shaded? Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.75, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 1e-06, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u06s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "3 parts, 1 shaded? Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 1e-06, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u06s1m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many thirds make a whole?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u06s1m05", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Fraction parts must be…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "equal", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "different", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m3u06s1m06", "type": "num", "prompt": "5 parts, 5 shaded? Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 1.0, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 1e-06, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c3u06", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 6.1 notes · Fractions of shapes", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "6.2", "title": "Equivalent fractions of shapes", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Two chocolate bars", "p": ["Bar A is cut into **2** equal pieces; you eat **1**. Bar B (same size) is cut into **4**; you eat **2**.", "Did you eat more of bar A or bar B? Think before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Halves and quarters", "p": ["A quarter is half of a half."], "qq": {"id": "m3u06s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many quarters in a half?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "2."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Equivalent fractions", "p": ["**Equivalent fractions** are the same amount even though they look different."], "fig": {"kind": "cells", "cells": [[0, 0, "#9EC1F2", ""], [1, 0, "#9EC1F2", ""], [2, 0, "#FFFFFF", ""], [3, 0, "#FFFFFF", ""]], "cols": 4, "rows": 1}, "p2": ["2/4 of this bar is shaded – the same as **1/2**. You ate the same amount of each bar."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "More equivalents", "p": [], "table": {"head": ["Fraction", "Equivalent"], "rows": [["1/2", "2/4, 3/6, 4/8, 5/10"], ["1/4", "2/8"], ["1/5", "2/10"], ["3/4", "6/8"]]}, "p2": ["Cutting each piece into 2 doubles both numbers: 1/2 → 2/4."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Equivalent", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m3u06s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "1/2 = ?/10", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "5."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I find equivalent fractions?", "p": ["Step 1: Draw two same-size bars.", "Step 2: Shade the first fraction.", "Step 3: Cut the second into more equal parts and shade the same amount.", "Step 4: Or double the top and the bottom."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Halves", "p": [], "q": "1/2 = ?/6.", "steps": [["6 is 3 × 2", ""], ["1 × 3", ""]], "a": "3/6"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Quarters", "p": [], "q": "1/4 = ?/8.", "steps": [["double", ""]], "a": "2/8"}, {"k": "example", "t":